.\" Manpage for bashcards.
.\" Contact me@robertwpearce.com to correct errors or typos.
.TH BASHCARDS 1 "2026-09-22" "bashcards 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bashcards \- practice flashcards in bash
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bashcards
.BR \-d | \-\-dir
.I DIRECTORY
.br
.B bashcards
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.br
.B bashcards
.BR \-v | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bashcards
is a bash program for practicing flashcards in bash.
It lists the decks (*.bcrds files) in a directory and lets you pick one.
It then shows each card in a random order: one side, then the other when
you press return.
Which side comes first is random, too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-d, \-\-dir " DIRECTORY
Directory containing bashcard files (*.bcrds).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
See this help information
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Current version
.SH DECK FILES
A deck is a UTF-8 text file named
.IR something .bcrds
with one card per line, formatted as
.IR front = back .
Everything after the first
.B =
is the back of the card, so a back may contain
.B =
but a front may not.
Blank lines are ignored.
Lines without an
.B =
are skipped with a warning.
.PP
For example, spanish.bcrds:
.PP
.RS
.nf
Te quiero.=I love you.
Hasta luego.=See you later.
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Card borders are measured in characters, so
.B bashcards
expects a UTF-8 locale
.RB ( LC_ALL ,
.B LC_CTYPE
or
.BR LANG )
and warns when it finds anything else.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B bashcards
exits 0 when you finish a deck or leave with ctrl-d.
It exits 1 when given an unknown option, no directory, a directory that
does not exist, or a directory without any *.bcrds files.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bashcards \-d ~/flashcards
.fi
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/rpearce/bashcards/issues
